[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    31[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   bounds are compile-time constants and not input-dependent);
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    32[0m:[38;5;10m[49m * no enum parameter, so there is no out-of-range-enum input class;
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    33[0m:[38;5;10m[49m * no length/size/count parameter, so there is no zero-length or oversized-length
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    34[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   input class.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    35[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    36[0m:[38;5;10m[49m Both entry points are total functions of a single `int`: **every** `int` value is
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    37[0m:[38;5;10m[49m a valid input, and neither can reject anything. Therefore the error-surface table
